※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4560

※ `from` names the parameter whose lifetime the answer borrows, so it names a
※ parameter of this function and nothing else.  A local would be no help -- it
※ is gone when the call is -- and a variable at the top level is what `static`
※ is for, so the only thing `from` can usefully point at is already the only
※ thing it is allowed to point at.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6

fn first(a: &u8) → &u8 from b:
    a
